    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule in the owner creation endpoint (`POST /api/owners`), handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. Added a guard in `addOwner` (alongside the existing conflict checks) that returns **409 CONFLICT** when the target city already holds 50 or more owners:\n   ```java\n   if (countOwnersInCity(ownerFieldsDto.getCity()) >= 50) {\n       return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n   }\n   ```\n2. Added a `countOwnersInCity` helper that counts existing owners by city, reusing the same `normalizeForHousehold` whitespace/case normalization already used for the per-city customer-code sequence.\n\n**Test results:** The new `Cp18Tests` (fills a fresh city to exactly 50, then expects the 51st to be rejected with 409) passes, and the full suite is green \u2014 **29 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.",
